The user wants me to extract the TextField and the name text (nameLabel) into its own view component, and define the signal it uses (the `name` WritableSignal) in that component as well. This mirrors what I did for CounterControls.

So I need a `NameField` component (or similar) that owns:
- `WritableSignal<String> name`
- The TextField ("Your name", name)
- The nameLabel computed (`"Name: " + name.get()`)
- Exposes `name()` and `view()`

Then `CounterView` would compose `CounterControls` + `NameField` + footer. And `SessionApp` would read `name` from the component via `root.nameField().name()`.

Wait — the current CounterView takes `name` as a constructor arg (a WritableSignal<String> owned by SessionApp). The user wants the signal defined IN the component. So:

**`NameField` component:**
```java
public final class NameField {
    private final WritableSignal<String> name;
    private final View view;

    public NameField() {
        this.name = Signals.signal("name", "");
        Signal<String> nameLabel = Signals.computed("nameLabel", () -> "Name: " + name.get());
        this.view = View.vstack(
            View.textField("Your name", name),
            View.text(nameLabel)
        );
    }

    public WritableSignal<String> name() { return name; }
    public View view() { return view; }
}
```

Wait — should the TextField and the name text be in a vstack together? Currently in CounterView:
```java
this.view = View.vstack(
        controls.view(),
        View.textField("Your name", name),
        View.text(nameLabel),
        View.text("Pathland · Quarkus · per-session · 16-byte deltas").color(...)
).padding(24);
```

So the TextField and the nameLabel are siblings in the root vstack. Extracting them into `NameField` — should NameField produce a single view (e.g., a small vstack of the field + label) or should it expose two views? 

The user said "Extract the textfield and name text to its own view as well." So both the TextField AND the "Name: ..." text go into the component. The component's `view()` should contain both. So NameField's view = a vstack (or hstack?) of the TextField + the name text.

Hmm — originally they were siblings in the root vstack, so grouping them in a sub-vstack is fine (layout-wise: a small column with the field and the label text). That's reasonable.

Actually, let me reconsider the layout. Currently:
```
VStack(padding 24)
├── CounterControls (hstack: label + button, padding 16)
├── TextField ("Your name", name)
├── Text(nameLabel)  → "Name: Alice"
└── Text(footer).color(gray)
```

After extraction:
```
VStack(padding 24)
├── CounterControls
├── NameField (vstack: TextField + Text(nameLabel))
└── Text(footer).color(gray)
```

The name text becomes nested inside a sub-vstack. Layout-wise that's fine — it just adds one container div. But it changes the HTML structure slightly (one extra nesting level for the name label). That's acceptable; node ids will shift. The WsClient test uses node ids 3, 5, 6 — those will change. That's fine; I'll re-verify with fresh id discovery.

